  <div class="apj-inst">
    <h2 class="apj-h2">The Aparajita Institution</h2>
    <p>Aparajita has celebrated women whose courage, resilience, and achievements have transformed lives and communities. Through these journeys, one belief became stronger than ever&mdash;that <b>every extraordinary child deserves a chance to grow, thrive and learn.</b></p>
    <p>The Aparajita Institution, located at <b>Baruipur</b>, was born on <b>14th April, 2026</b> on the occasion of Ambedkar Jayanti. Established by <b>Sanmarg Foundation</b> in partnership with <b>Nishtha Foundation</b>, the institution is dedicated to empowering children, women, and families from underserved communities through education, opportunity, and holistic development.</p>
    <div class="apj-stats">
      <div class="apj-stat">
        <p class="apj-stat-num">20,000</p>
        <p class="apj-stat-label">Girls to begin with</p>
      </div>
      <div class="apj-stat">
        <p class="apj-stat-num">2 Lakh</p>
        <p class="apj-stat-label">Lives to be impacted</p>
      </div>
      <div class="apj-stat">
        <p class="apj-stat-num">14.04.2026</p>
        <p class="apj-stat-label">Born on Ambedkar Jayanti</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>At the institution, children receive <b>free education</b> alongside English communication, digital literacy, health and hygiene awareness, sports, arts, creativity, mindfulness, and essential life skills. Supported by trained educators, nutritious meals, healthcare support, transportation facilities, libraries, and computer learning centres, the institution prepares children not just for examinations, but for a dignified and purposeful life.</p>
    <p>The institution&rsquo;s vision extends beyond the classroom. Mothers and women from the community are actively engaged through <b>skill development and livelihood programmes</b> including stitching, weaving, handicrafts, pottery, jewellery-making, menstrual hygiene awareness, and financial empowerment initiatives&mdash;creating opportunities for women to become self-reliant and economically independent, and to support the education of their children.</p>
    <p>Beginning with 20,000 girls and aiming to impact over 2 lakh lives, The Aparajita Institution aims to create lasting, generational change&mdash;where every child is given free education and the opportunity to learn, every woman is empowered to grow, and every family is supported to thrive.</p>
